Trying to prove your value is one of the fastest ways to lose it.

A lot of people think being kind means being endlessly patient. Always understanding. Always giving the benefit of the doubt. But over time, that turns into something else.

It teaches people that access to you has no cost.

Disrespect rarely comes out of nowhere. It grows in the space where boundaries were never made real. When nothing changes after the line gets crossed, the message is loud even if you never say a word.

Kindness is not the same thing as self erasure. Having a good heart does not mean accepting behavior that slowly trains you to shrink.

Respect is built through what you allow, what you correct, and what you walk away from. Not through how nice you sound while being overlooked.

If someone keeps crossing your line, it is usually because that line was never enforced in the first place.
